Track 1: "Who Poured Hot Palm Oil on the Permafrost?"
- Story & Context: In the sub-zero depths of Svalbard Core 4, agronomist Mateo knocked an illegal kerosene burner during an unauthorized shift meal, sending smoking red palm oil and roasted shallots scorching across the sub-zero iron flooring and cracking the glass cases of dormant Andean barley. The sudden thermal hiss and sizzling aroma caused the facility's panic klaxons to wail, prompting the shift crew to drown out the sirens by banging metal soup ladles against steel vault doors and singing highlife harmonies to calm the shocked grain embryos. As the aroma of hot oil mingled with sub-zero freezer vapor, Mateo belted the opening hook into the ventilation intake: "Boil the broth until the frozen seeds remember the sun!" Within thirty minutes, acoustic sensors registered thousands of microscopic root radicles bursting from their husks in rhythm with the conga tumble.
