Track 2: Abena's Braised Peanut Caldo
- Story & Context: Alone during a forty-day polar night, seed curator Abena Osei confessed into the vault audio logs that she was covertly rerouting voltage from the permafrost chillers into an industrial stockpot to simmer roasted peanut paste, scotch bonnets, and wild yams. Her knuckles were stained with turmeric and garlic paste as she wept over the sleeping grain trays, overwhelmed by the silence of the Arctic winter. To keep from unraveling, she leaned her head against the cold steel racks and sang a sweeping, multi-tracked vocal prayer that coaxed tiny green leaves through the wire mesh trays: "Taste the cumin on my tongue, little grain, and do not die in the dark." The resulting recording captured her layered backing vocals soaring over montuno piano chords played on a smuggled electric keyboard, permanently thawing Chamber B into an unofficial communal sanctuary.
